            <ArticleTitle>Metal-free decarbonylative alkylation-aminoxidation of styrene derivatives with aliphatic aldehydes and N-hydroxyphthalimide.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1338-1342</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob00030h</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A convenient metal-free decarbonylative alkylation-aminoxidation of styrene derivatives with aliphatic aldehydes and N-hydroxyphthalimide (NHPI) to yield phthalimide protected alkoxyamines is developed. With DTBP as an oxidant and radical-initiator, this reaction smoothly converts aliphatic aldehydes into alkyl radicals and subsequently allows the cascade construction of C(sp3)-C(sp3) and C(sp3)-O bonds via radical-radical coupling.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
